#
# The cost J (code_tap/cost_atlantic_heat.F): the northward volume transport
# across one grid row, in Sverdrups, integrated from the surface over
# cost_atl_kmaxdepth levels, averaged over the final lastinterval (default 30 d)
# of the run (a shorter run averages over its own length), mult_atl times.
# Since 2026-10-29; until then the routine kept the tree's form, which divided
# each MPI tile's sum by the tile's wet-cell count, so J was about 1/16.6 of the
# transport (and a 5-day run reported one sixth of that): a run's build_info.txt
# says which with cost_units=Sv, absent for the old form.
#
# The section is a namelist setting since 2026-10-20 (a parameter statement in
# the source until then, so that a section meant a build): cost_atl_jsec is the
# 1-based row whose SOUTHERN face is integrated across, named by the row's
# centre, and cost_atl_kmaxdepth the number of levels. The sections in use, and
# the interface each integrates to (input_tap/data delR):
#     26 N   cost_atl_jsec=127  cost_atl_kmaxdepth=25  (982 m)   every run up to job 31434
#     43 N   cost_atl_jsec=148  cost_atl_kmaxdepth=24  (848 m)   the overturning maximum: production since 2026-10-13
#     60 N   cost_atl_jsec=175  cost_atl_kmaxdepth=25  (982 m)   subpolar, the OSNAP latitudes (2026-10-20)
#     25 S   cost_atl_jsec=74   cost_atl_kmaxdepth=24  (848 m)   north of the Deacon cell (2026-10-20)
# IMPACTS_COST_JSEC and IMPACTS_COST_KMAXDEPTH override the two per run from the
# environment (tools/lib/submit_body.sh); the run directory's name carries the
# section (_sec43N, ...) and its staged copy of this file is the record.
# analyses/DINO_1deg/adjoint/kappa_v_ensemble_gmFwd/overturning_maximum.py has the
# streamfunction behind the choices.
#
# ******************
# cost function
# ******************
 &COST_NML
  mult_atl = 1.,
  cost_atl_jsec = 148,
  cost_atl_kmaxdepth = 24,
 &
